course: dictionary
lesson: 14108
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context tells you which one the writer means. Look at capital letters, the words near the word, and what the sentence is about. «A merlin swooped low over the moor and caught a small bird.» Swooping and catching birds are things a bird does, so a merlin here is an animal.
explain: Now read this: «Merlin the wizard gave young Arthur wise advice.» The capital M and the word wizard show that Merlin is a name, a character from old legends. A bird cannot give advice to a king, so this is not the bird meaning.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. A capital letter often means a name, but always read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: A merlin is a small, fast falcon, a bird of prey.
fact: Merlins live in Europe, Asia and North America, often on moors and open land.
fact: A merlin hunts small birds by chasing them fast.
fact: «Merlin» with a capital letter is a name: the wise wizard in the stories of King Arthur.
fact: In the legends, Merlin guides and advises Arthur, and helps him become king.
exercise: «A merlin dived past the hedge and caught a small finch.» What is a merlin here? | *A small, fast falcon | A wise old wizard | A type of hedge | A king in a story
exercise: «Merlin the wizard whispered wise words to young Arthur.» Who is Merlin in this sentence? | A fast chase across the moor | *A wizard from the legends | A castle on the hill | A small bird that hunts finches
exercise: «The merlin flew over the moor, hunting for small birds.» What tells you this merlin is a bird? | Its name starts with a capital letter | *It hunts small birds | It is a wizard with a long beard | It lives in a castle
test: «Merlin told the young king to trust his heart.» What is Merlin here? | A stone with a sword in it | A small, fast falcon | A kind of moor | *A wise wizard in the legends
test: «A merlin is one of the smallest falcons.» What is a merlin? | *A small falcon, a bird of prey | A wizard in old stories | A name for a king | A large wild cat
exam: «Merlin gave the king a magic sword.» Which meaning fits this sentence? | *The wizard in the legends | A small, fast falcon | A moor where birds nest | A hedge full of finches
